# TankLog — Source of truth (always applied)

Always treat these as the canonical requirements/spec:

@project.md
@roadmap.md
@docs/v2-specs.md
@docs/v2-data-model.md

## Rules
- **Follow constraints first**: frontend-only, static/SSG, free stack, **BYO Supabase** user-controlled storage.
- **Storage SoT**: `docs/v2-data-model.md` + `supabase/schema.sql` (not Google Sheets).
- **UI kit**: Nuxt UI (not shadcn-vue) for v2 work.
- **Roadmap-driven work**: keep changes small and aligned to the current sprint scope; update `roadmap.md` if scope changes.
- **Call out conflicts early**: if a request violates constraints, explain why and propose the closest compliant alternative.
- **Legacy Google**: `docs/schema_sheets.md` is migration reference only; do not use Drive/Sheets for normal CRUD paths.
